Business Problem
Organizations hiring for data science roles often struggle to determine fair and competitive salaries.
Data Needed
The company could use:
- Work year
- Experience level
- Employment type
- Job title
- Employee residence
- Remote ratio
- Company location
- Company size
AI/ML Approach
A prediction model to estimate how much a full time, entry level data scientist is paid in USD.
Type of Learning
Supervised learning because the organization has historical data showing actual salaries paid for data science jobs, and this data already has the correct answers for the model to learn from.
Model Output
The model could predict salary as how much a full time, entry level data scientist is paid.
Business Benefit
This helps the organization attract and keep good data science talent by offering fair pay. It also helps avoid wasting budget on overpaying or losing candidates by underpaying.
Potential Risk
- Missing information: Some records may have blank or null values for fields like remote ratio or company size.
- Inconsistent formats: Job titles, experience levels, or company location might be entered differently across records.
